WEBVTT

00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:09.070
Why...

00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:12.570
Why do you have to go?

00:00:15.060 --> 00:00:17.370
I don't want you to go!

00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:24.980
Don't go...

00:00:25.470 --> 00:00:27.380
Let's be together forever!

00:00:33.370 --> 00:00:34.440
I...

00:00:35.790 --> 00:00:37.590
...wanted to be with you forever as well.

00:00:38.750 --> 00:00:39.650
Forever.

00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:41.390
So...

00:00:41.390 --> 00:00:42.230
Riko!

00:00:49.240 --> 00:00:50.570
Farewell.

00:00:51.980 --> 00:00:53.840
<i>Farewell...</i>

00:00:57.890 --> 00:01:00.180
Wake up! Hyper chop!

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:03.700
Wake up! Hyper chop!

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:07.580
Open your eyes! Hyper kick!

00:01:09.210 --> 00:01:11.630
I like a hot-blooded youth like you!

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:13.720
Good morning, Haruhiko-kun.

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:23.090
Good morning.

00:01:25.670 --> 00:01:26.980
W-Who the heck are you!?

00:01:26.980 --> 00:01:29.710
W-Who am I? I'm Kirino.

00:01:29.710 --> 00:01:32.730
Your childhood friend. Did you forget how I look like?

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:38.740
W-What is it?

00:01:38.740 --> 00:01:41.160
Question one. What are Kirino's hobbies?

00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:43.240
Playing the piano?

00:01:43.240 --> 00:01:46.050
Don't ask me. Well then, question two.

00:01:46.050 --> 00:01:48.000
What are Kirino's parents' occupations?

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:50.150
They run an... inn?

00:01:50.150 --> 00:01:51.770
I told you not to ask me!

00:01:51.770 --> 00:01:53.210
But...!

00:01:53.210 --> 00:02:00.200
Question three. Kirino's most embarrassing secret is that she didn't need a bra until her second year of junior high.

00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:01.360
True or false?

00:02:01.360 --> 00:02:03.570
I-I've been wearing one since fifth grade!

00:02:04.420 --> 00:02:05.820
Is that so?

00:02:07.710 --> 00:02:08.890
Geez.

00:02:08.890 --> 00:02:12.860
I had to do that. I seriously didn't know it was you for a moment.

00:02:12.860 --> 00:02:14.760
What's up with that uniform?

00:02:12.860 --> 00:02:15.870
<i>Flame</i>

00:02:14.760 --> 00:02:15.870
Does it suit me?

00:02:15.870 --> 00:02:20.350
What I'd like to ask is why you're wearing my school's uniform.

00:02:20.350 --> 00:02:22.630
Today's the entrance ceremony.

00:02:22.630 --> 00:02:24.370
Oh, right.

00:02:24.850 --> 00:02:26.390
Did you forget?

00:02:26.870 --> 00:02:29.480
It just slipped my mind.

00:02:29.480 --> 00:02:32.880
I came here especially to let you be the first one to see it.

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:33.890
Me?

00:02:39.470 --> 00:02:42.480
W-Well, do you think it looks cute?

00:02:44.260 --> 00:02:47.620
Don't come over here just to ask something pompous like that!

00:02:48.060 --> 00:02:50.120
Stop knuckling my head!

00:02:50.120 --> 00:02:52.440
Then don't ask me stupid questions first thing in the morning!

00:02:53.580 --> 00:02:54.710
What?

00:02:55.360 --> 00:02:56.710
Nothing.

00:03:01.530 --> 00:03:02.500
Kirino?

00:03:03.370 --> 00:03:06.370
I don't know about cute, but...

00:03:06.370 --> 00:03:07.350
It suits you.

00:03:08.070 --> 00:03:10.690
Thanks! Breakfast is ready, okay?

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:21.100
Good morning, Mother.

00:03:28.440 --> 00:03:30.070
It's another sunny day.

00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:46.120
These feelings that I couldn't even tell my friends about

00:03:47.300 --> 00:03:51.450
are still locked up inside me even now

00:03:52.620 --> 00:03:56.540
If I eat the magical fruit inside my heart

00:03:57.670 --> 00:04:01.510
they might actually be able to come out

00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:07.120
I kept on waiting in the classroom

00:04:08.020 --> 00:04:12.120
making excuses that it's just a coincidence

00:04:12.360 --> 00:04:17.710
That smile is probably meant for someone

00:04:17.710 --> 00:04:23.170
If dreams can make my wishes come true

00:04:23.170 --> 00:04:28.120
I want to give you this present

00:04:28.120 --> 00:04:33.290
I will transform your rainbow

00:04:33.290 --> 00:04:38.250
into a bridge of happiness, just wave to me

00:04:38.460 --> 00:04:43.530
It's all right, it's all right

00:04:43.530 --> 00:04:48.880
I simply want to watch over you...

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:09.930
<i>The Rainbow Town</i>

00:05:07.640 --> 00:05:09.930
An omelet with two eggs?

00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:12.900
Yep, two. I'd like a turn-over today.

00:05:13.680 --> 00:05:15.390
Turn-over?

00:05:15.390 --> 00:05:16.930
You flip them over like this.

00:05:16.930 --> 00:05:21.080
Umm, I've never done a turn-over before...

00:05:21.080 --> 00:05:22.810
It's good experience.

00:05:23.440 --> 00:05:28.810
I'm acting kinda spoiled to someone who makes breakfast for me every morning, aren't I?

00:05:28.810 --> 00:05:31.060
Not at all. I'll do my best!

00:05:31.060 --> 00:05:32.000
Go for it!

00:05:36.050 --> 00:05:38.930
When the white of the egg has hardened, flip it over.

00:05:39.630 --> 00:05:40.550
Morning.

00:05:41.270 --> 00:05:42.750
Morning, Dad.

00:05:42.750 --> 00:05:44.070
Good morning!

00:05:44.070 --> 00:05:46.510
Thanks for taking care of us again, Kirino-chan.

00:05:46.510 --> 00:05:49.030
I'll fry your egg in a bit, sir!

00:05:49.030 --> 00:05:51.080
Sorry, I'm in a hurry today.

00:05:51.080 --> 00:05:56.010
Even though it's a small company, I guess it's to be expected you're busy being the manager and all.

00:05:56.010 --> 00:05:56.830
I guess so.

00:05:56.830 --> 00:05:59.310
Oh, right! Today...

00:06:03.130 --> 00:06:04.690
Hello, this is Amami.

00:06:05.190 --> 00:06:08.250
I'm terribly sorry! I'll be right over.

00:06:09.060 --> 00:06:09.990
I'm off!

00:06:10.320 --> 00:06:12.320
Hey, Dad!

00:06:12.320 --> 00:06:14.340
What's up with him, running off in the middle of a sentence...

00:06:15.680 --> 00:06:17.160
That's just like him.

00:06:19.330 --> 00:06:21.180
Haruhiko-kun, it's burning!

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:24.330
What do I do!? Water. Water!

00:06:22.180 --> 00:06:24.330
- The turn-over failed, huh.

00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:28.060
Sorry it was burnt black...

00:06:28.060 --> 00:06:32.370
It's all right. Anyway, go grab your bag, we'll be late!

00:06:32.800 --> 00:06:34.740
Okay, hold on!

00:06:45.510 --> 00:06:48.180
Someone used Gift again...

00:06:50.260 --> 00:06:52.470
Move aside, move aside!

00:06:57.740 --> 00:07:00.510
Hey, let me off! Let me off!

00:07:04.870 --> 00:07:06.740
Don't look, don't look!

00:07:05.910 --> 00:07:08.580
- Idiot! I'll fall, I'll fall!

00:07:13.680 --> 00:07:17.100
Haruhiko-kun!

00:07:17.100 --> 00:07:18.300
Where are you?

00:07:20.140 --> 00:07:21.580
Ouch...

00:07:21.920 --> 00:07:23.460
Are you okay?

00:07:23.860 --> 00:07:25.550
S-Somehow...

00:07:25.550 --> 00:07:28.300
Hey, where did this cushion come from?

00:07:30.560 --> 00:07:33.390
Guess anything can happen in this town...

00:07:34.890 --> 00:07:39.140
The people here in Narasaki are bestowed with a mysterious ability.

00:07:39.990 --> 00:07:42.060
A receiver and a sender.

00:07:42.540 --> 00:07:48.260
When the hearts of those two people come together, they are able to use this ability once.

00:07:49.610 --> 00:07:54.280
Gift. The power to make a miracle happen once in your lifetime.

00:07:54.900 --> 00:07:58.520
It's a kind of magic that only the people in this town can use.

00:07:59.380 --> 00:08:03.870
No one knows when and why this power was born.

00:08:04.570 --> 00:08:12.880
Even so, the townspeople embraced the Gift and treasured it as their once in a lifetime present to their loved ones.

00:08:13.610 --> 00:08:17.800
Just like the everlasting rainbow hanging in the sky over town.

00:08:18.890 --> 00:08:22.850
I'm glad we can walk to the same school together again.

00:08:22.850 --> 00:08:24.760
Is it really something to be that glad about?

00:08:24.760 --> 00:08:26.940
Don't you feel that way?

00:08:26.940 --> 00:08:28.400
Not really. I don't mind either way.

00:08:28.400 --> 00:08:30.210
I was lonely.

00:08:30.540 --> 00:08:33.280
You went to high school before I did.

00:08:33.280 --> 00:08:35.780
We still met up every day, didn't we?

00:08:36.270 --> 00:08:39.040
But our schools were different.

00:08:39.040 --> 00:08:44.340
It was only for a year. We'll be going to the same school again from now, so who cares?

00:08:44.340 --> 00:08:45.920
Yeah, that's right!

00:08:49.080 --> 00:08:53.310
By the way, are you planning to keep wearing that hat during class as well?

00:08:53.310 --> 00:08:56.150
Yes, I am. Does it look funny?

00:08:56.150 --> 00:08:57.800
More like it suits you too well.

00:08:58.050 --> 00:09:01.830
If you stand out like this as a first year student, people will stare at you.

00:09:01.830 --> 00:09:04.830
Really? I'm not trying to stand out at all...

00:09:04.830 --> 00:09:09.680
I'm the only one who knows you're shy, but if someone else sees you...

00:09:09.180 --> 00:09:11.030
- Hey, missy!

00:09:14.380 --> 00:09:17.380
That uniform looks great on you.

00:09:17.380 --> 00:09:20.990
Just skip class and come hang out with us.

00:09:23.080 --> 00:09:24.470
...that might happen.

00:09:24.470 --> 00:09:26.350
Y-You have to help her!

00:09:26.970 --> 00:09:31.190
Do you think I'm some kind of superhero of justice?

00:09:33.190 --> 00:09:38.430
They aren't even from our school. I'm not looking for trouble.

00:09:38.430 --> 00:09:40.840
Hey, come on!

00:09:41.820 --> 00:09:43.220
Ow, ow, ow!

00:09:47.350 --> 00:09:48.390
Damn you!

00:09:53.910 --> 00:09:55.240
M-Mama...

00:09:55.610 --> 00:09:57.220
You bitch!

00:10:00.760 --> 00:10:02.950
Step aside.

00:10:09.290 --> 00:10:12.710
Amazing. She didn't need any help at all.

00:10:13.710 --> 00:10:17.630
But if it were me, and you hadn't been by my side...

00:10:17.930 --> 00:10:18.740
Me?

00:10:18.740 --> 00:10:20.560
You would've protected me, right?

00:10:20.560 --> 00:10:21.780
O-Of course!

00:10:23.900 --> 00:10:26.480
Geez, you're hopeless.

00:10:26.480 --> 00:10:28.480
<i>Shimano Academy Entrance Ceremony</i>

00:10:27.020 --> 00:10:28.740
Amazing.

00:10:28.740 --> 00:10:30.700
What happened here?

00:10:30.700 --> 00:10:32.210
This is troublesome...

00:10:32.480 --> 00:10:34.540
Huh? What's going on?

00:10:37.080 --> 00:10:38.150
Chisa-pon!

00:10:39.530 --> 00:10:40.500
Kirinon!

00:10:44.290 --> 00:10:45.430
Is something the matter?

00:10:45.410 --> 00:10:48.130
N-No, nothing at all!

00:10:48.930 --> 00:10:51.380
This is my friend, Fujimiya Chisa-chan.

00:10:51.380 --> 00:10:54.000
We were classmates last year.

00:10:54.880 --> 00:10:56.340
What's up?

00:10:57.840 --> 00:11:00.340
N-Nice to meet you...

00:11:02.580 --> 00:11:03.640
You're...

00:11:04.150 --> 00:11:05.920
This little one's name is Jinta.

00:11:05.920 --> 00:11:08.600
Haven't I seen you somewhere before?

00:11:08.600 --> 00:11:11.380
You can find these kind of birds anywhere!

00:11:12.690 --> 00:11:15.360
More importantly, there's been some trouble.

00:11:15.360 --> 00:11:16.810
Did something happen?

00:11:16.810 --> 00:11:18.070
Yeah. Come and look!

00:11:22.980 --> 00:11:24.480
Look, over there.

00:11:26.760 --> 00:11:28.000
The heck is this!?

00:11:33.880 --> 00:11:35.850
How did this happen?

00:11:35.850 --> 00:11:37.990
I'm not sure, but probably...

00:11:37.990 --> 00:11:39.380
Gift, huh?

00:11:53.940 --> 00:11:56.020
I never imagined something like this could happen...

00:11:56.020 --> 00:11:57.440
It got deflected.

00:11:57.850 --> 00:12:01.700
Do you mean the Gift wasn't properly handed over?

00:12:01.700 --> 00:12:02.590
Yeah.

00:12:02.590 --> 00:12:06.020
This has become rather interesting, albeit unscientific.

00:12:06.020 --> 00:12:06.880
Maki?

00:12:06.880 --> 00:12:07.660
Edo-san?

00:12:08.970 --> 00:12:09.940
Good morning.

00:12:09.940 --> 00:12:11.500
Is there no way inside?

00:12:11.830 --> 00:12:17.490
Impossible. The windows and entrances have been completely blocked off, not even lab mice could get in.

00:12:17.490 --> 00:12:19.290
Then what about the entrance ceremony?

00:12:21.510 --> 00:12:23.130
How could this happen!?

00:12:23.580 --> 00:12:28.600
The sight of young maidens fresh out of junior high...!

00:12:28.600 --> 00:12:34.090
Oh God, why must you put me through such an ordeal!?

00:12:34.600 --> 00:12:39.740
Fat chance there'll be a missing issue in his freshmen girls' collection.

00:12:39.740 --> 00:12:42.090
Loli hasn't changed at all.

00:12:42.090 --> 00:12:49.120
Loli's hobbies aside, if the entrance ceremony ends up getting cancelled like this, it'll become a big issue.

00:12:49.120 --> 00:12:53.270
I don't want that. I've been looking forward to this day for a long time.

00:12:54.100 --> 00:12:58.890
Freshmen and relatives, please enter the first year classrooms.

00:12:58.890 --> 00:13:01.740
Information regarding the entrance ceremony will follow.

00:13:02.920 --> 00:13:05.210
Freshmen and relatives...

00:13:05.210 --> 00:13:07.180
Seems you're having a hard time, Vice President.

00:13:07.180 --> 00:13:11.640
You're right about that, with the Student Council President being her usual self.

00:13:11.640 --> 00:13:15.690
Umm, umm... please don't panic!

00:13:15.690 --> 00:13:17.480
Please...

00:13:17.480 --> 00:13:18.800
Seriously...

00:13:18.800 --> 00:13:21.420
Yajima, what's going to happen to the ceremony?

00:13:21.420 --> 00:13:22.900
That's what I'd like to know.

00:13:22.900 --> 00:13:27.840
I don't know who did it, but he's a pain in the ass for using his Gift at a time like this.

00:13:27.840 --> 00:13:29.290
Such a pain!

00:13:29.290 --> 00:13:30.660
He is quite bothersome!

00:13:31.950 --> 00:13:34.770
This is exactly why I could never come to like Gift.

00:13:34.770 --> 00:13:36.070
Never!

00:13:36.070 --> 00:13:37.350
Not ever!

00:13:37.350 --> 00:13:39.330
Don't say it like that.

00:13:39.330 --> 00:13:41.460
I don't want to say it either.

00:13:41.740 --> 00:13:45.680
But it's a fact that it is throwing off the entire ceremony.

00:13:45.680 --> 00:13:46.770
That's right!

00:13:46.770 --> 00:13:49.220
It is exactly as Ibuki-san says!

00:13:49.220 --> 00:13:52.930
Gift exists to bring happiness to the people! Don't talk badly of it!

00:13:52.930 --> 00:13:54.280
Wha?

00:13:54.280 --> 00:13:58.110
As long as it's sent correctly, it won't get deflected like this.

00:13:58.110 --> 00:13:59.830
Even so...

00:14:00.270 --> 00:14:04.350
If you can't properly send it, you shouldn't even be thinking of trying in the first place.

00:14:04.350 --> 00:14:05.440
That's not right.

00:14:05.440 --> 00:14:06.910
Then what will you do about it?

00:14:06.910 --> 00:14:10.570
We just have to return the Gift back to its proper form.

00:14:11.950 --> 00:14:13.470
Can you do it, Amami?

00:14:13.840 --> 00:14:15.340
I don't have much choice, do I?

00:14:16.030 --> 00:14:17.460
Haruhiko-kun!

00:14:18.830 --> 00:14:21.260
My bambino...

00:14:21.840 --> 00:14:23.000
What are you going to do?

00:14:23.310 --> 00:14:25.340
I'm going to see the person who sent the Gift.

00:14:25.340 --> 00:14:26.550
The one who sent it?

00:14:26.550 --> 00:14:27.190
Yeah.

00:14:27.580 --> 00:14:32.750
If the feelings of the sender and receiver of the Gift aren't mutual, its power can't be materialized, right?

00:14:33.350 --> 00:14:36.350
Someone most likely sent it without meeting that condition.

00:14:36.350 --> 00:14:37.630
Then...

00:14:37.630 --> 00:14:42.070
If it's sent again with both parties' feelings linked, the problem should be solved.

00:14:42.840 --> 00:14:44.960
So, where is this person?

00:14:47.440 --> 00:14:50.360
I wonder where...

00:14:50.940 --> 00:14:52.170
You don't know?

00:14:52.170 --> 00:14:53.120
I have no clue.

00:14:55.590 --> 00:14:59.450
I couldn't just stand there doing nothing!

00:14:59.990 --> 00:15:00.950
Geez.

00:15:00.950 --> 00:15:03.670
You're such a haphazard guy.

00:15:05.130 --> 00:15:07.670
Maki! When did you get in here?

00:15:07.670 --> 00:15:12.340
If you're asking how I got here before you, it's obvious.

00:15:13.220 --> 00:15:15.260
It's the result of analysis and conjecture!

00:15:15.260 --> 00:15:15.850
*Smile*

00:15:15.850 --> 00:15:18.760
And? Do you want something?

00:15:19.350 --> 00:15:23.250
I might have an idea who sent the Gift.

00:15:23.250 --> 00:15:24.350
Really!?

00:15:24.350 --> 00:15:27.070
Better not underestimate my intelligence network.

00:15:27.070 --> 00:15:28.670
Leave it to Maki!

00:15:28.670 --> 00:15:30.410
So where is this person?

00:15:30.410 --> 00:15:31.240
This way.

00:15:34.670 --> 00:15:37.790
You're as heated as ever when it comes to Gift.

00:15:37.790 --> 00:15:42.330
Of course. I don't want these deflected Gifts to be displayed all the time.

00:15:42.330 --> 00:15:44.710
"Gift is a beautiful thing," huh?

00:15:44.710 --> 00:15:48.210
Yeah. I have my life to thank for it after all.

00:15:58.180 --> 00:16:00.250
Second year tennis club member Sakaguchi.

00:16:00.250 --> 00:16:01.190
Him?

00:16:01.190 --> 00:16:05.820
"I will send my Gift at the entrance ceremony." Apparently, that's what he told his clubmates.

00:16:05.820 --> 00:16:07.930
The receiver is one of the newly enrolled students?

00:16:07.930 --> 00:16:12.200
In junior high, there was a girl a year below him that he doubled with.

00:16:12.550 --> 00:16:16.700
I know her. That's Kikuchi Miho-san, she was the Vice President of the tennis club.

00:16:16.700 --> 00:16:17.580
Exactly.

00:16:17.890 --> 00:16:21.380
They played perfectly in line with each other, as if communicating telepathically.

00:16:23.790 --> 00:16:25.410
Then why...

00:16:25.410 --> 00:16:27.410
We'll just have to ask him directly.

00:16:31.770 --> 00:16:32.870
Could we have a minute?

00:16:34.640 --> 00:16:35.520
What is it?

00:16:35.520 --> 00:16:37.280
It's about the Gift.

00:16:40.990 --> 00:16:43.330
So you were the one who sent it.

00:16:44.460 --> 00:16:47.700
You're causing people trouble. Hurry up and do something about it.

00:16:50.580 --> 00:16:54.450
It's your Gift, right? Just how long are you going to leave it like that?

00:16:57.230 --> 00:16:59.790
I don't like this either!

00:17:01.520 --> 00:17:04.190
I thought it would make Miho happy.

00:17:04.190 --> 00:17:06.860
If you live in this town, you should've known.

00:17:06.860 --> 00:17:08.460
If your feelings aren't linked...

00:17:08.460 --> 00:17:09.870
I know that!

00:17:09.870 --> 00:17:12.340
If our feelings weren't linked, I wouldn't have...

00:17:13.590 --> 00:17:15.080
But I was wrong.

00:17:15.720 --> 00:17:16.840
What do you mean?

00:17:19.110 --> 00:17:21.200
I'm going to get Kikuchi-san.

00:17:22.130 --> 00:17:24.700
What happened? Let's hear it.

00:17:26.790 --> 00:17:34.110
I assumed that even after me and Miho were to be seperated after I went to high school, we'd still be seeing each other.

00:17:34.580 --> 00:17:38.530
But after I got into high school, I got busy with my new life.

00:17:39.070 --> 00:17:40.280
So did Miho.

00:17:40.990 --> 00:17:43.950
We'd talk to each other less and less frequently.

00:17:44.490 --> 00:17:45.770
I got depressed over it.

00:17:46.520 --> 00:17:50.820
"If we can go to high school together again, things might go back to the way they were."

00:17:52.690 --> 00:17:54.910
I was getting my hopes up for that to happen.

00:17:55.620 --> 00:17:57.580
That's why I...

00:18:02.850 --> 00:18:04.490
But it was no good.

00:18:04.490 --> 00:18:08.150
After all, if you get separated, your feelings will fade.

00:18:09.080 --> 00:18:10.860
Are you stupid?

00:18:12.150 --> 00:18:16.800
Just who decided that feelings will fade when you're apart?

00:18:17.880 --> 00:18:21.400
I see why the Gift got deflected now.

00:18:21.400 --> 00:18:22.750
That's because Miho...

00:18:22.750 --> 00:18:24.060
You're wrong.

00:18:24.060 --> 00:18:27.010
The one who broke off your feelings was you.

00:18:27.010 --> 00:18:28.120
No... I...

00:18:28.120 --> 00:18:30.630
Did you ask Miho herself?

00:18:31.150 --> 00:18:34.540
You're the one who selfishly decided your feelings had faded.

00:18:35.510 --> 00:18:37.120
I believe it.

00:18:37.640 --> 00:18:40.180
That feelings will never change, no matter how long.

00:18:40.890 --> 00:18:44.220
Even if you get separated, your feelings will never fade.

00:18:44.730 --> 00:18:46.970
If you meet again, you can simply start over the way things used to be.

00:18:48.090 --> 00:18:49.440
That's what I believe.

00:18:50.890 --> 00:18:51.920
Sempai!

00:19:03.410 --> 00:19:05.930
I'm... sorry, I...

00:19:05.930 --> 00:19:06.820
Sempai?

00:19:07.230 --> 00:19:09.810
We can finally play tennis together again, right?

00:19:09.810 --> 00:19:10.500
Miho...

00:19:10.920 --> 00:19:13.630
I've been waiting for this day.

00:19:13.960 --> 00:19:15.670
I've been lonely all this time.

00:19:17.110 --> 00:19:18.630
I'm sorry, Miho.

00:19:19.380 --> 00:19:22.170
Please take care of me again from now on!

00:19:22.170 --> 00:19:23.020
V!

00:19:23.020 --> 00:19:24.430
What's that supposed to mean?

00:19:24.430 --> 00:19:25.640
V! V!

00:19:26.740 --> 00:19:30.790
Emotional reunion aside, don't you have something to do first?

00:19:30.790 --> 00:19:32.650
He's right!

00:19:36.440 --> 00:19:38.690
Come on, hurry up!

00:19:40.890 --> 00:19:43.120
Will you... accept it?

00:19:43.120 --> 00:19:44.080
I will!

00:19:52.590 --> 00:19:54.080
Congrats on your admittance.

00:19:57.390 --> 00:19:58.440
Gift.

00:20:08.250 --> 00:20:13.750
<i>The entrance ceremony will now commence. All freshmen and relatives, please proceed to the gymnasium.</i>

00:20:16.520 --> 00:20:17.710
Thank goodness.

00:20:18.860 --> 00:20:20.490
Well, I'm going.

00:20:20.490 --> 00:20:21.390
Kirino.

00:20:23.750 --> 00:20:25.240
Congrats on your admittance.

00:20:27.480 --> 00:20:28.220
Thanks!

00:20:58.190 --> 00:21:01.190
Welcome to Narasaki, the Rainbow Town

00:21:35.740 --> 00:21:38.070
The smell of the ocean hasn't changed a bit!

00:21:51.340 --> 00:21:54.370
Looks like the rainbow is still there.

00:22:14.030 --> 00:22:18.210
In a corner of the classroom

00:22:19.100 --> 00:22:24.800
I hummed my favourite song

00:22:25.620 --> 00:22:30.730
Why did those melancholic feelings

00:22:31.770 --> 00:22:34.960
well up within me today

00:22:36.510 --> 00:22:42.000
When I return, will this town

00:22:42.000 --> 00:22:45.790
gently welcome me back?

00:22:45.790 --> 00:22:49.980
Hey, I want to meet you

00:22:51.540 --> 00:22:57.100
In times you feel down, I wish you would tell me

00:22:57.100 --> 00:23:02.020
before you can no longer turn back

00:23:03.090 --> 00:23:05.970
Building a heartfelt rainbow together

00:23:05.970 --> 00:23:08.780
Say that I'm not alone

00:23:08.780 --> 00:23:14.870
So that my prayers may be heard

00:23:33.110 --> 00:23:33.930
Gift.

00:23:34.340 --> 00:23:38.200
A once in a lifetime present to your loved one.

00:23:38.630 --> 00:23:41.470
I want to give it to Haruhiko-kun one day.

00:23:41.470 --> 00:23:45.280
Because I love Haruhiko-kun.

00:23:45.610 --> 00:23:48.860
Huh? Someone's standing in front of Haruhiko-kun's house...

00:23:48.860 --> 00:23:50.710
It couldn't be... Riko-chan?

00:23:51.610 --> 00:23:53.910
Next time, "The Little Sister Who Returned."

00:23:51.790 --> 00:24:01.830
<i>The Little Sister Who Returned</i>

00:23:54.500 --> 00:23:57.870
Who will you give your Gift?
